erhero movies again because they've  been killed previously but that's  ridiculous how can just one bad film of  a specific strength of superhero lead to  digits not happening for over a decade  because there's not enough of them  the fewer that there are the more  important each individual one becomes  it's basic physics it's the district  it's the distribution of weight it's the  principle that a bed of nails works on  the more points of contact that there  are the less pressure there is on each  individual one if there is only one  point of contact all of the pressure is  on that one point of contact and in this  case if I were to step out of the  metaphor the pressure in this case is  the pressure to be good now the pressure  on all of those other 53 male lead films  was all fairly low some were great some  were terrible but they didn't have to be  good any one of those could fail and the  genre wasn't something going to go away  because there was plenty of other points  of contact there was plenty of weight to  distribute the weight of and the  importance of this genre across all  these films so one could fail HEC 10  could fail it wasn't going to kill the  genre but when you narrow it down to the  more specific sub-genre of female led  superheroes it's just Wonder Woman and  if that had failed he could have killed  it and we'd seen that happen before and  if you want to even take it out of the  gender context you go back to Batman or  Robin which many people blamed for  killing superhero movies at the time and  you know there were some that were made  within a few years of it but really kind  of effectively as far as big-budget  superhero movies when it did kill it but  the reason that it was able to kill it  if there was not nearly as many  superhero movies coming out at that time  Batman pretty much was the stand  Bearer because other superhero movies  either hadn't really gotten off the  ground yet or hadn't connected and so  when the franchise carrying the weight  of the superhero genre failed that was  kind of it for a bit but at this point  we don't need that anymore even Batman  which I would say is still the premier  franchise of super in among superheroes  Batman the new Batman film could be  awful I hope it's not but it could be  superheroes aren't going to go anywhere  in terms of their presence in film  because there's so many of them so when  I say proportional representation if the  number of female led superheroes was  even close to the proportion of women in  the perspective audience then we  wouldn't have to worry whether or not  one film like Wonder Woman manages to be  all things all people manages to be  exciting enough manages to be feminist  that we wouldn't have to worry about  that because if we had more women  superheroes then we could have one that  is very much a strongly feminist  character we could have one that is more  acting masculine and sort of playing in  the boys club kind of thing we could  have one that tackles things from a more  uniquely female perspective as opposed  to just solving all the problems with  punching we could have a diversity of it  if there was just more places to do it  the other thing that's worth bringing up  is how weird again the conversation got  about Black Widow in age of Ultron and  the thing that happened with a storyline  there and again I don't really want to  get into whether or not what was done  specifically in terms of revealing that  she wasn't able to have kids and the  impact that had on her as a character I  don't necessarily want to get into  whether or not that was a good thing or  not but the conversation that happened  that basically said ah see they reduced  her her value to the fact that she can't  be a mother therefore she thinks she's a  mobster bah sexism and again I don't  want to say whether or not that is  sexist but I don't think it's a  conversation that would have  had to happen if she wasn't literally  the girl of the marvel and s